<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Communication ability: it holds the conversation, admits
  communication input into it, and says the response the cognition selects
  through Speaking.
  The body (bots/floppy/floppy.scx) invokes it as its child
  "communication".

    communication { inactive -children ready-> active
                    active -respond-> admitting_response -> preparing_response
                      -> dispatching_response
                      -> responding { waiting } -speaking output, failure or
                      hop timeout-> active }

  Children: communication holds <invoke id="conversation"> (abilities/
  conversation/conversation.scx, the one active conversation) and <invoke
  id="speaking"> (abilities/speaking/speaking.scx). Each is ready when it
  sends bot.ability.ready; inactive waits for both. A child that cannot
  start, or ends, sends
  bot.ability.communication.failed {message} to the body and ends this
  ability in its final state degraded.

  Input: bot.ability.communication.input {source_ids, target_ids, content,
  content_type, ...} in active or responding (hearing goes on while a
  response is said, decision D175) goes to the conversation as
  bot.ability.conversation.routed_input {parent} (the input routed to the
  active conversation; parent is the input event as an envelope). The
  conversation hands a text product over as bot.ability.cognition.input
  {stimulus}, which goes on to the body unchanged (the body grants it a
  turn); its bot.ability.conversation.output goes on to the body unchanged
  when its latest message is inbound (a product that is not text) and is
  the exchange only otherwise; and its bot.ability.conversation.failed
  {stage, message} goes on to the body unchanged.

  Responding: bot.ability.communication.respond {parts} in active (decision
  D178: 1 to 64 parts {expression?, words?}, each with
  words, a sound or a pause, every expression directing a cue, and the
  words, joined exactly as written, not blank; a respond that breaks one is
  refused with bot.ability.communication.failed) numbers the response
  (preparing_response), sends bot.ability.speaking.input {parts} to the
  speaking child
  (dispatching_response), and waits in responding's waiting, bounded by
  the hop timer bot.ability.communication.response.hop.timed_out
  (response_timeout_ms, 36 s: speaking's 30 s encoding bound plus 6 s,
  decision D98; the transition takes only the timer of the response in
  hand, _event.sendid). Each bot.ability.speaking.progress
  {spoken_seconds} re-enters waiting, which re-arms the timer (decision
  D179), so a long spoken reply is never cut off; until the first audio no progress comes, so the
  first hop still covers the whole encoding. Speaking's output goes on to
  the body as bot.ability.speaking.output. A speaking failure
  (bot.ability.failed) or the hop timeout answers the body with
  bot.ability.communication.failed {message}; the timeout also sends
  speaking bot.ability.speaking.stop {}, so it does not go on saying a
  response whose failure was already reported (decision D179). Input that arrives in
  inactive is held by <event:defer/> (scxml.rs namespaces/event) and comes
  back, in order, on the return to active. A response's id is its
  respond's sendid (none when the sender named none); leaving responding
  retires it into the last closed_responses_bound (16) finished ids, and a
  respond for a finished id, or another copy of the one in hand or of a
  held one (held_ids), is dropped and logged (communication.late). Other responses that arrive
  while one is in hand are held by <event:defer/>, up to
  held_responses_bound (16); past that one is refused with
  bot.ability.communication.failed (decision D175). Held
  responses come back, in order, on the return to active, where they are
  taken as on arrival; a response in inactive is not taken (inactive has no
  transition for it).

  Stop: bot.ability.communication.stop {} (model-callable, decision D179)
  is taken only in responding, so it is offered only while a response is
  being spoken: it sends bot.ability.speaking.stop {} to speaking, which
  stops the utterance in hand (an SCXML <send> takes no id from an
  expression, so the stop cannot carry the response's id; speaking holds
  one utterance at a time), and re-enters waiting; speaking's output
  (outcome "stopped") ends the response as any other.

  Speaking's routes: speaking records the words it said as an outbound
  bot.ability.conversation.append, which the communication passes to the
  conversation (a sibling is out of speaking's reach), and its playout,
  bot.ability.speaking.efference and then environment.sound, is passed on
  in order whatever the state: the copy to the body, the sound into the
  environment, at #_scxml_ + the <data> environment (the environment's id,
  the body's <param>; decision D103, amended 2026-10-15: the communication
  puts the sound into the environment, after the copy has left for the
  body, so the copy reaches the listening first). Speaking's copy of the
  bot's own voice, bot.ability.listening.enroll, goes to the body too
  (for its Listening), and the body's bot.ability.listening.enrolled
  goes to speaking, whatever the state.

  Activate: bot.ability.communication.activate {} keeps the one
  conversation active (a catalog of conversations to switch between is
  loaded through memory, phase 3); it is taken and logged in inactive only.

  Offers: the move from inactive into active sends bot.ability.ready to
  the body, once (decision D242). What it offers, the body reads from its
  live session with <decision:offers>: the events its offerable <data>
  declares, of no effort, while a transition without a cond takes them:
  in active respond (activate is taken only in inactive, and input is not
  declared), whose one transition admits it in admitting_response (a late
  copy of a finished response is dropped there, a reply that says nothing
  refused); in responding respond (held) and stop. The children offer
  nothing.

  Contracts: the events it takes reference abilities/schemas/ by
  event:schema (never inline). scxml.rs checks them where each event is
  created: a send whose data a schema rejects is not routed and raises
  error.execution in its sender. Each event it takes has one sender, so
  its name and the active state route it; conds only correlate (which
  timer) and keep the non-blank response check (decision D178).

  Bindings: speaking's (the conversation namespace and vocal's speech
  service).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="communication" initial="communication">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="response_timeout_ms" expr="36000"/>
    <!-- Speaking's encoding bound, passed to it (decision D98). -->
    <data id="encoding_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <!-- The memory database file, for the conversation (null:
         no memory). -->
    <data id="database" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The environment's id (decision D106), where speaking's sound goes. -->
    <data id="environment" expr="null"/>
    <data id="ready" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- The response in hand: its number, words, id (its respond's
         sendid, null when the sender named none) and hop timer. -->
    <data id="operation" expr="0"/>
    <data id="response" expr="null"/>
    <data id="response_id" expr="null"/>
    <data id="hop_timer" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The ids of the last closed_responses_bound responses that finished,
         so a late copy of one never reopens it, and how many other
         responses are held while one is said (decision D175). -->
    <data id="closed_responses_bound" expr="16"/>
    <data id="closed_responses" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="held_responses_bound" expr="16"/>
    <data id="held" expr="0"/>
    <data id="held_ids" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="failure" expr="null"/>
    <!-- What it offers its parent (decision D242), which reads it from its
         live session with <decision:offers>: respond in active and
         responding, stop in responding, both of no effort. -->
    <data id="offerable" expr="({'bot.ability.communication.respond': {}, 'bot.ability.communication.stop': {}})"/>
    <!-- The children. -->
    <data id="children" expr="['conversation', 'speaking']"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="communication.js"/>

  <state id="communication" initial="inactive">
    <invoke id="conversation" type="scxml" src="../conversation/conversation.scx">
      <param name="database" expr="database"/>
    </invoke>
    <invoke id="speaking" type="scxml" src="../speaking/speaking.scx">
      <param name="encoding_timeout_ms" expr="encoding_timeout_ms"/>
    </invoke>

    <!-- A child's readiness, once (decision D242), named by its invoke id. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.ready" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.ready.json">
      <assign location="ready[_event.invokeid]" expr="true"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- Conversation products go on to the body: a text product as its
         stimulus handoff, any other whose latest message is inbound as
         the output itself; the rest is the exchange only. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.cognition.input.json">
      <log label="communication.product" expr="productTurn(_event)"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.output.json">
      <log label="communication.exchange" expr="exchangeLength(_event)"/>
      <if cond="isInboundProduct(_event)">
        <send event="bot.ability.conversation.output" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </if>
    </transition>
    <!-- A snapshot of the conversation's participants (the communication
         requests none). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.snapshot.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.snapshot.output.json">
      <log label="communication.snapshot" expr="_event.data.request_ref"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- A conversation that could not take an input fails it (its
         bot.ability.conversation.failed, forwarded unchanged). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.failed.json">
      <log label="communication.rejected" expr="conversationFailedLog(_event)"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.conversation.failed" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <!-- A child that cannot run, or ends, degrades the ability. -->
    <transition event="error.*" target="degraded">
      <assign location="failure" expr="childRunFailure(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="done.invoke.conversation done.invoke.speaking" target="degraded">
      <assign location="failure" expr="childEndFailure(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- Speaking's record of what it said, and its playout: the copy to
         the body, then the sound into the environment, in the order speaking
         sent them, so the copy is in the body's queue before the
         environment can deliver the sound back (decision D103, amended
         2026-10-15). -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.append" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.conversation.append.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.conversation.append" target="#_conversation">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.efference.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <!-- Speaking's copy of the bot's own voice goes to the body, for its
         Listening; the Listening's answer comes back to speaking. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.listening.enroll" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.listening.enroll.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.listening.enroll" target="#_parent">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.listening.enrolled" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.listening.enrolled.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.listening.enrolled" target="#_speaking">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="environment.sound" event:schema="../schemas/environment.sound.json">
      <send event="environment.sound" targetexpr="environmentTarget()">
        <content expr="_event.data"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <!-- Hearing goes on whatever is being said: input in active or
         responding goes to the conversation (taken in both, decision
         D175); inactive holds it. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.conversation.routed_input" target="#_conversation">
        <param name="parent" expr="routedParent(_event)"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <!-- A speaking answer, or progress, for no response in hand. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.output bot.ability.speaking.progress bot.ability.failed">
      <log label="communication.stale" expr="_event.name"/>
    </transition>

    <!-- Waits for the conversation and speaking. A child that cannot
         start raises its error with no invokeid (SCXML 6.4.2). -->
    <state id="inactive">
      <!-- Ready, once (decision D242). -->
      <transition cond="childrenReady()" target="active">
        <send event="bot.ability.ready" target="#_parent"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="degraded">
        <assign location="failure" expr="childStartFailure(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json">
        <event:defer/>
        <log label="communication.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.activate" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.activate.json">
        <log label="communication.activate" expr="'conversation'"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- Its one respond transition has no cond, so it is what the parent
         reads as the offer (decision D242); admitting_response decides. -->
    <state id="active">
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.respond" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.respond.json"
                  target="admitting_response">
        <assign location="response" expr="_event.data.parts"/>
        <assign location="response_id" expr="responseId(_event)"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- A late copy of a finished response is dropped, and a reply that
         says nothing is refused; any other is said. -->
    <state id="admitting_response">
      <transition cond="isClosedAdmission()" target="active">
        <log label="communication.late" expr="response_id"/>
        <assign location="response" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="response_id" expr="null"/>
      </transition>
      <transition cond="isSpokenAdmission()" target="preparing_response"/>
      <transition target="active">
        <log label="communication.rejected" expr="'bot.ability.communication.respond needs parts that say something'"/>
        <assign location="response" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="response_id" expr="null"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.communication.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="'A reply must say something: every part needs words, a sound or a pause, and the words must not be blank.'"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- The response is numbered. -->
    <state id="preparing_response">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="operation" expr="nextOperation()"/>
      </onentry>
      <transition target="dispatching_response"/>
    </state>

    <!-- The response goes to speaking. -->
    <state id="dispatching_response">
      <onentry>
        <send event="bot.ability.speaking.input" target="#_speaking">
          <param name="parts" expr="response"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition target="responding"/>
    </state>

    <!-- Waits for speaking's answer, bounded while speaking shows no
         progress. -->
    <state id="responding" initial="waiting">
      <onexit>
        <assign location="closed_responses" expr="closedResponses()"/>
        <assign location="response_id" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="held" expr="0"/>
        <assign location="held_ids" expr="[]"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.output.json" target="active">
        <send event="bot.ability.speaking.output" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="active">
        <send event="bot.ability.communication.failed" target="#_parent">
          <param name="message" expr="_event.data.message"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- A late copy of a finished response, or another copy of this one,
           is dropped, as is another copy of a held one; another response is
           held, up to held_responses_bound. One transition without a cond,
           so the parent reads it as an offer (decision D242). -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.respond" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.respond.json">
        <if cond="isLateResponse(_event)">
          <log label="communication.late" expr="_event.sendid"/>
        <elseif cond="canHold()"/>
          <event:defer/>
          <assign location="held" expr="held + 1"/>
          <assign location="held_ids" expr="heldIds(_event)"/>
          <log label="communication.deferred" expr="_event.name"/>
        <else/>
          <log label="communication.rejected" expr="heldOverMessage()"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.communication.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="'Communication is holding too many responses; this one is refused.'"/>
          </send>
        </if>
      </transition>

      <!-- A stop while the response is said (taken here, not in waiting, so
           it is offered while responding): speaking stops it, and waiting
           starts again for its answer. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.stop" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.stop.json"
                  type="internal" target="waiting">
        <log label="communication.stop" expr="operation"/>
        <send event="bot.ability.speaking.stop" target="#_speaking">
          <content expr="({})"/>
        </send>
      </transition>

      <!-- Re-entered on every sign of progress, which restarts the hop
           timer. -->
      <state id="waiting">
        <onentry>
          <send idlocation="hop_timer" event="bot.ability.communication.response.hop.timed_out" delayexpr="responseTimeoutDelay()">
            <param name="operation" expr="operation"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendidexpr="hop_timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.progress" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.progress.json" target="waiting"/>
        <transition event="bot.ability.communication.response.hop.timed_out" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.communication.response.hop.timed_out.json"
                    cond="isResponseHopTimeout(_event)" target="active">
          <log label="communication.hop.timed_out" expr="hopTimedOutMessage()"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.speaking.stop" target="#_speaking">
            <content expr="({})"/>
          </send>
          <send event="bot.ability.communication.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="'Speaking response timed out.'"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- A child could not run: the ability ends (the body degrades). -->
  <final id="degraded">
    <onentry>
      <log label="communication.degraded" expr="failure"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.communication.failed" target="#_parent">
        <param name="message" expr="failure"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
  </final>
</scxml>
